From 31e4b1c4b37e4fcd23b30ebb2cce64e25360bba7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiraWells <1020080523@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 08:13:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(witness): record positional state-read witnesses while
 executing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A witness is the sequence of values a block's execution read from state —
account by account, slot by slot, in the order a fresh revm `State` sent
them to its database — and nothing else: no keys, no code, no block
hashes. A re-executor runs the block against a fresh `State` whose
database answers each read with the next value in the stream, so every
block of the chain replays on its own, in parallel, with no state and no
lookups.

The execution stage runs blocks through one long-lived `State` whose
cache carries values across blocks, so the reads it sends to the provider
are not the reads a fresh `State` would send. The recorder therefore
keeps a fresh `State` of its own per block, offers it every read the
batch `State` answers, and lets that fresh `State`'s cache decide which
reads reach a database — the same decision, taken by the same code, the
replayer's fresh `State` will take. Commits are mirrored so the shadow
evolves through the block as the replayer's will. Nothing imitates the
cache; anything the shadow cannot account for fails the block loudly.

- vendor/revm-database: revm-database 42.0.0 plus `State::read_observer`,
  a `StateReadObserver` told of every `basic`/`storage` answer and every
  committed account, in order. Patched over crates.io; identical
  otherwise (one method made public).
- crates/witness (`reth-witness`): the stream format, an on-disk store
  (`witness.idx` + 2 GiB `witness.NNNN.dat` segments, per-block zstd,
  resumable at the execution checkpoint, unwound with execution), the
  recorder, and `replay_block` / `WitnessDb` for stateless re-execution.
- `Executor::{set_read_observer, read_observer_mut}` with defaults;
  `BasicBlockExecutor` and `Either` implement them.
- `ExecutionStage::with_witness_dir`, `ExecutionConfig::witness_dir`
  (`[stages.execution]` in reth.toml) and `--debug.witness-dir`.

Tested: the stream and store round-trip; a three-block chain built to hit
cross-block cache hits, a contract created in an earlier block, an
account first absent then created, reads inside a reverting call and
withdrawals records under the batch executor and replays block by block
from a fresh state with identical receipts, passing post-execution
validation; a foreign or tampered witness does not; the execution stage
with a witness dir records a block that replays without state.
